From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:32:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] sync: settle mutations covered by an earlier transition

A covering query transition can arrive before its mutation response. The
request manager previously waited for another transition even when the
applied snapshot already included the write, retaining the pending promise
and optimistic update unnecessarily.

Complete successful responses when their commit timestamp is at or before
the current connection's applied query timestamp. Reuse the existing
completion bookkeeping and query notification path so optimistic updates
are removed before promise continuations run. Keep waiting when query state
is behind the commit. Do not use the maximum observed timestamp: mutation
responses advance it and it survives reconnects while query state resets.

Report alreadyApplied on response_received only when that response settles
a tracked success. Do not invent transition receipt or application events.
Document the consistency boundary in production comments and the patch
index. This changes no wire protocol or backend behavior.

Cover equal and later snapshots, insufficient coverage, reconnect replay,
duplicate responses, listener exceptions, and optimistic cleanup with
tracing disabled. The focused sync suite passes all 64 tests; SDK typecheck,
focused ESLint, and the full package build also pass.
